# Composer installs a release from GitHub's archive of the tag, and the archive holds only what this
# allow-list keeps: the PHP half - its code (php/src), its migration files (php/migrations) and its
# resources (php/resources) - with composer.json, README.md and CHANGELOG.md. Everything else stays out,
# a folder added later too: the Angular workspace, the tests, the workflows. Every site's build uploads
# vendor/ whole. CI builds the archive and checks the list (.github/scripts/check-archive.sh).
/* export-ignore
/php !export-ignore
/php/tests export-ignore
/composer.json !export-ignore
/README.md !export-ignore
/CHANGELOG.md !export-ignore

# What a release ships to be read byte for byte has LF line endings in every checkout and archive: a
# migration's last line is read (Japanese Academy's draft rule), and a test holds the SQL to the words.
/php/migrations/** text eol=lf
/php/resources/** text eol=lf

# A shell script with CRLF line endings does not run.
/.github/scripts/*.sh text eol=lf
